From: SF2000 Linux Port <sf2000-linux@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: sf2000: keep backlight dark until userspace

The loader provides the one normal-boot health blink and finishes with the
backlight disabled. Early kernel progress is retained in RAM and on UART, so
turning the backlight on at every milestone only exposes inherited ST7789 GRAM
before the display service is ready to own the panel.

Keep both nonblocking progress helpers dark. The userspace display owner turns
the backlight on when it starts the physically proven panel transaction.

--- a/arch/mips/kernel/setup.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/setup.c
@@ -649 +649 @@ void sf2000_visible_stage(const char *name, unsigned int pulses)
-	sf2000_backlight_set(1);
+	sf2000_backlight_set(0);
@@ -664 +664 @@ void sf2000_visible_tick(const char *name)
-	sf2000_backlight_set(1);
+	sf2000_backlight_set(0);
